@model ImagePolicyEditorModel
@{ ViewData["Title"] = "Image update policy"; }
<h1>Image update policy</h1>
<form method="post" action="/automation/images/edit">@Html.AntiForgeryToken()
<div asp-validation-summary="All"></div><input asp-for="Id" type="hidden" /><input asp-for="Revision" type="hidden" />
<label asp-for="Name"></label><input asp-for="Name" />
<label asp-for="DeploymentId"></label><input asp-for="DeploymentId" />
<label asp-for="Services">Compose service names (comma-separated)</label><textarea asp-for="Services"></textarea>
<label asp-for="Mode"></label><select asp-for="Mode"><option value="notify-only">Notify only (record available updates; no redeploy)</option><option value="auto-deploy">Redeploy through normal pipeline and verify health</option></select>
<label asp-for="FrequencyMinutes">Check frequency (minutes, 1–525600)</label><input asp-for="FrequencyMinutes" type="number" min="1" max="525600" />
<label asp-for="FailureBackoffMinutes">Retry after failure (minutes, 1–525600)</label><input asp-for="FailureBackoffMinutes" type="number" min="1" max="525600" />
<label><input asp-for="Enabled" /> Enabled</label><button>Save image policy</button></form>
<p>Checks compare immutable SHA-256 image digests resolved for the Agent platform, with scoped registry credentials supplied only by the normal operation pipeline. Locally built services are excluded unless they have an explicitly configured registry source. Unknown current digests never trigger automatic deployment.</p>
<p>Checks do not overlap for a policy. Redeployments use the normal deployment operation queue, coordinating with builds, Git updates and scheduled deployments. Missing digest-probe support or registry errors produce a failed check, never a fabricated success. Notify-only updates appear in the automation overview.</p>
